.TH PSORT 1 "2026-05-17" "psort" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
psort.pl \- count input lines, sort by frequency, and display with percentages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B psort.pl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B psort.pl
reads lines from standard input or one or more files, counts the occurrences
of each unique line, and prints them sorted by frequency from least to most
common (or most to least common with
.BR \-r ).
Each output line shows the percentage of the total, the raw count, and the
value.  A
.B Total:
line is printed at the end.
.PP
It is equivalent to
.BR "sort | uniq \-c | sort \-n" ,
but with cleaner formatting, percentages, and additional filtering options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-csv
Output in CSV format
.RI ( "percentage%,count,value" )
instead of the human-readable aligned columns.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-csvall
Like
.BR \-\-csv ,
and also replace all whitespace within each value with commas.
.TP
.BR \-d " \fIN\fR, " \-\-decimal =\fIN\fR
Number of decimal places to use for percentages.  Default is
.BR 4 .
.TP
.B \-\-numeric
Sort by the numeric value of the input lines rather than by occurrence count.
Useful when input lines are numbers and you want them in numeric order.
.TP
.BR \-m " \fIN\fR, " \-\-min =\fIN\fR
Exclude entries whose count is below
.IR N .
Excluded counts are accumulated into an
.B [excluded]
summary line unless
.B \-\-ignore
is given.  By default the total and percentages are recomputed from the
remaining entries; see
.B \-\-fullperc
to override this.
.TP
.BR \-x " \fIN\fR, " \-\-max =\fIN\fR
Exclude entries whose count is above
.IR N .
Operates the same way as
.BR \-\-min .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fullperc
When used with
.B \-\-min
or
.BR \-\-max ,
compute percentages based on the full original total rather than the
count of the filtered entries.
Requires at least one of
.B \-\-min
or
.BR \-\-max .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore
When used with
.B \-\-min
or
.BR \-\-max ,
suppress the
.B [excluded]
summary line that would otherwise account for the filtered-out entries.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
When used with
.B \-\-min
or
.BR \-\-max ,
print to standard error the number of keys and total count before and after
filtering.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reverse
Reverse the sort order so the highest count (or highest numeric value with
.BR \-\-numeric )
appears first.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-histogram
Display a bar graph alongside each percentage, scaled to the terminal
width.  The bar column precedes the percentage so relative sizes are
immediately visible.  Ignored when
.B \-\-csv
or
.B \-\-csvall
is active.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH HISTOGRAM OUTPUT FORMAT
With
.BR \-H ,
each entry line is prefixed by a bar whose fill is proportional to the
entry's percentage of the total:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[\fIbar\fR] \fIpercentage\fR%  \fIcount\fR \fIvalue\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
The bar width is computed from the terminal width (via
.BR TIOCGWINSZ )
minus the fixed-width columns, so it fills available space.
If the terminal width cannot be determined, 80 columns is assumed.
The
.SB COLUMNS
environment variable overrides the detected width.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
Default (human-readable) output format per line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fIpercentage\fR%  \fIcount\fR \fIvalue\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Percentages below 10 are padded with a leading space so the decimal points
align.  The count column is right-justified to the width of the total count.
.PP
CSV output
.RB ( \-c " or " \-a ):
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fIpercentage\fR%,\fIcount\fR,\fIvalue\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
The final line in either format is:
.PP
.RS
.nf
  Total:  \fIN\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Count file extensions under the current directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
find . \-type f | sed 's/.*\\.//' | psort.pl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show the top 5 most common HTTP status codes (highest count first):
.PP
.RS
.nf
awk '{print $9}' access.log | psort.pl \-r | head \-5
.fi
.RE
.PP
Count word frequencies, keeping only words that appear at least 10 times:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tr \-cs 'A\-Za\-z' '\\n' < document.txt | tr 'A\-Z' 'a\-z' | psort.pl \-\-min 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show distribution of numeric response times, sorted by value:
.PP
.RS
.nf
awk '{print $NF}' timings.log | psort.pl \-\-numeric
.fi
.RE
.PP
Output a CSV of all entries whose count is between 5 and 100, using the
full total for percentages:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat data.txt | psort.pl \-c \-\-min 5 \-\-max 100 \-\-fullperc
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or empty input (no output produced).
.TP
.B 1
Invalid option combination (e.g.\&
.B \-\-fullperc
without
.B \-\-min
or
.BR \-\-max ).
.SH IMPLEMENTATIONS
Four implementations are provided, all supporting identical options:
.TP
.B psort.pl
Original Perl implementation.
.TP
.B psort_c
C implementation (fastest; uses an open-addressing hash table with FNV-1a
hashing).
.TP
.B psort_go
Go implementation.
.TP
.B psort.py
Python 3 implementation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sort (1),
.BR uniq (1),
.BR awk (1)
